{"seq":10,"slug":"cluster-analysis","title":"聚类分析","stage":"DONE","category":"data-science","chapterCount":4,"docCount":14,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis","rating":{"composite":4.04,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":5,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"聚类分析-简介\">聚类分析 简介</h1><p>面对一堆没有标签的数据——一群顾客、一批基因、一组文档——我们想问：它们之间是否隐藏着自然的分群？<strong>聚类分析</strong>正是回答这一问题的方法：在无人指导的&quot;无监督&quot;前提下，仅凭数据自身的相似与差异，发现潜藏的群组结构。它没有唯一正确答案，价值不在求标准解，而在帮我们发现数据中原本未知的结构与洞察。</p>\n<p>本知识库面向已具备基本数据分析素养、希望系统理解&quot;如何让数据自己分群&quot;的读者。它不绑定某一具体工具或库，聚焦于聚类的<strong>核心思想、相似性度量、主要算法、评估与应用</strong>这条贯穿始终的主线。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本-hub-与兄弟-hub-的分工边界\">本 hub 与兄弟 hub 的分工边界</h2><p>聚类分析与数据科学板块下若干 hub 主题相邻，但各有侧重。下表厘清边界，帮你判断该读哪一个：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>你的问题</th>\n<th>该读的 hub</th>\n<th>与本 hub 的关系</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>无标签数据如何自动分群</td>\n<td><strong>聚类分析（本 hub）</strong></td>\n<td>主题本体</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>高维数据该如何降到可处理/可视的维度</td>\n<td><a href=\"../dimensionality-reduction/\">降维</a></td>\n<td>聚类前常先降维以缓解维度灾难</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>如何找出不属于任何群组的异常点</td>\n<td><a href=\"../anomaly-detection/\">异常检测</a></td>\n<td>密度聚类顺带识别离群点，二者方法相通</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>脏数据、缺失值、尺度问题怎么处理</td>\n<td><a href=\"../data-cleaning-preprocessing/\">数据清洗与预处理</a></td>\n<td>聚类前的数据准备工序</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>如何构造与选择有判别力的特征</td>\n<td><a href=\"../feature-engineering/\">特征工程</a></td>\n<td>特征质量决定聚类成败</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>把分群结果画出来、讲清楚</td>\n<td><a href=\"../data-visualization/\">数据可视化</a></td>\n<td>验证与解读聚类结果的工具</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>用相似度给用户推物品</td>\n<td><a href=\"../recommender-systems/\">推荐系统</a></td>\n<td>相似性度量的工业应用</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>一句话区分：<strong>降维</strong>改变数据的表示、<strong>清洗与特征工程</strong>准备数据、<strong>异常检测</strong>找出格格不入者，而本 hub 专注于&quot;把相似的归为一群&quot;这件事本身。</p>\n<h2 id=\"推荐学习路径\">推荐学习路径</h2><p><strong>初次接触聚类（建议按章顺序通读）</strong>：第一章建立整体认知与&quot;无监督&quot;视角 → 第二章理解相似性这一基石 → 第三章掌握主要算法 → 第四章上升到评估、应用与意义。这是为该 hub 设计的默认路径。</p>\n<p><strong>只想快速会用 k 均值的实践者</strong>：直读 <a href=\"similarity-and-distance/scaling-standardization\">尺度与标准化</a> → <a href=\"clustering-algorithms/partitioning-kmeans\">划分式聚类与 k 均值</a> → <a href=\"evaluation-and-application/choosing-cluster-number\">确定簇数</a>，足以跑通一次客户细分。</p>\n<p><strong>已懂算法、关心&quot;结果可不可信&quot;的分析师</strong>：重点读第四章，尤其 <a href=\"evaluation-and-application/evaluation-metrics\">聚类质量的评估</a> 与 <a href=\"evaluation-and-application/challenges-pitfalls\">聚类的挑战与陷阱</a>——它们直面&quot;算法强加的假象&quot;这一最危险陷阱。</p>\n<p><strong>做高维数据（文本、图像、基因）的读者</strong>：先补 <a href=\"../dimensionality-reduction/\">降维</a> 中的维度灾难，再回到第二章理解为何高维下距离会失效。</p>\n<h2 id=\"前置知识\">前置知识</h2><ul>\n<li><strong>基本数据素养</strong>：理解&quot;对象—特征&quot;的数据表格、数值/类别等特征类型。</li>\n<li><strong>初等几何直觉</strong>：把对象看作空间中的点、用距离衡量远近——第二章会从零讲起，无需线性代数基础。</li>\n<li><strong>概率的朴素概念</strong>（仅第三章高斯混合一节用到）：理解&quot;以多大概率属于某簇&quot;即可，不要求掌握具体分布。</li>\n<li><strong>无需</strong>任何编程或特定库基础；本 hub 讲思想与方法，不绑定实现。若需动手，可配合 <a href=\"../data-science-overview/\">数据科学总览</a> 中的 Python 生态一节。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>阅读时不妨始终把握一条主线：聚类是在无人指导下，让数据依其内在相似性自己分群——它没有唯一正确答案，其价值在于帮我们发现数据中潜藏的、原本未知的结构与洞察。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"clustering-foundations","title":"第一章 聚类基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/clustering-foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"what-is-clustering","title":"什么是聚类","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/clustering-foundations/what-is-clustering"},{"seq":2,"slug":"unsupervised-learning","title":"无监督学习的本质","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/clustering-foundations/unsupervised-learning"},{"seq":3,"slug":"clustering-workflow","title":"聚类的基本流程","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/clustering-foundations/clustering-workflow"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"similarity-and-distance","title":"第二章 相似性与距离","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/similarity-and-distance","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"distance-measures","title":"距离度量","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/similarity-and-distance/distance-measures"},{"seq":2,"slug":"similarity-metrics","title":"相似性度量的多样","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/similarity-and-distance/similarity-metrics"},{"seq":3,"slug":"scaling-standardization","title":"尺度与标准化","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/similarity-and-distance/scaling-standardization"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"clustering-algorithms","title":"第三章 聚类算法","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/clustering-algorithms","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"partitioning-kmeans","title":"划分式聚类与 k 均值","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/clustering-algorithms/partitioning-kmeans"},{"seq":2,"slug":"hierarchical-clustering","title":"层次聚类","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/clustering-algorithms/hierarchical-clustering"},{"seq":3,"slug":"density-clustering","title":"密度聚类","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/clustering-algorithms/density-clustering"},{"seq":4,"slug":"other-methods","title":"其他聚类方法","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/clustering-algorithms/other-methods"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"evaluation-and-application","title":"第四章 评估与应用","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/evaluation-and-application","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"evaluation-metrics","title":"聚类质量的评估","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/evaluation-and-application/evaluation-metrics"},{"seq":2,"slug":"choosing-cluster-number","title":"确定簇数","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/evaluation-and-application/choosing-cluster-number"},{"seq":3,"slug":"challenges-pitfalls","title":"聚类的挑战与陷阱","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/evaluation-and-application/challenges-pitfalls"},{"seq":4,"slug":"applications-significance","title":"应用与意义","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/cluster-analysis/evaluation-and-application/applications-significance"}]}]}